00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:05.580
I'm on a farm with Josh Groban.

490
00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:08.080
And I'm like, all these people have been watching for years.

491
00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:09.280
It's just such a weird.

492
00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.100
Where am I?

493
00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.040
Yeah, did someone like dose me with acid?

494
00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:16.340
And I'm like, just back in my basement apartment in Hell's Kitchen

495
00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:17.840
having like a weird fever dream.

496
00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:18.660
Yeah.

497
00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:21.520
So I watched like your first couple of episodes,

498
00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:26.180
which must have been so insane because you're talking about being new and everything.

499
00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:26.680
Right.

500
00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:31.780
So like there's the scene where you enter Dunder Mifflin for the first time

501
00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:34.640
and Dwight is holding a giant tray of hot dogs.

502
00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:39.860
And then Aaron and Andy sing the Sabre song.

503
00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:40.540
Yes.

504
00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:42.100
That is so crazy.

505
00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:45.560
And then the next episode, you're like wrestling some Great Danes

506
00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:47.000
and you're talking to Kathy Bates.

507
00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:48.060
Kathy Bates.

508
00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:48.920
I know, that's crazy.

509
00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:49.180
Just right out.

510
00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:52.460
When did they tell you that you would be working with Kathy Bates?

511
00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:55.060
You know, this is not a satisfying answer,

512
00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:58.020
but the truth is, again, it's just this sort of like pummeling.

513
00:21:58.980 --> 00:21:59.780
Of anxiety.

514
00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:00.940
Yeah, like I don't even know.

515
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.880
I felt like I was like being beaten into a happy gang or something.

516
00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:06.520
And it's like, just like, it's just like, I don't know, like Kathy Bates,

517
00:22:07.100 --> 00:22:10.660
like the office, like you're driving and you're going to be like,

518
00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:14.740
it just felt like this kind of like word jumble of like, I don't know.

519
00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:15.240
What's next?

520
00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:15.560
Yeah.

521
00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:18.760
I just felt like, like, I don't remember finding it out.

522
00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:20.920
Like, it's like the fog of war.

523
00:22:21.160 --> 00:22:22.580
I'm just like, I don't remember.

524
00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:24.960
Like, that's very funny.

525
00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:28.240
We were so nervous about Kathy Bates being on set.

526
00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:28.660
Really?

527
00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:29.040
Oh my gosh.

528
00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:29.300
Yeah.

529
00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:30.240
What were you nervous about?

530
00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:31.280
Just that she would tell me.

531
00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:32.060
Just anything.

532
00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:33.980
Just like making eye contact.

533
00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:36.380
And she was such a presence.

534
00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:37.980
And then she was so kind.

535
00:22:37.980 --> 00:22:41.880
I think it was just her stature and her body of work.

536
00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:48.220
And we had avoided for so long having like these big name actors on the show.

537
00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:51.080
And so this was kind of a turning point.

538
00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:52.760
And it was very shocking.

539
00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:54.260
It felt like, you know.

540
00:22:54.420 --> 00:22:54.660
Yeah.

541
00:22:54.660 --> 00:23:00.060
So my hair colorist had once colored Kathy Bates' hair.

542
00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:00.900
This is genius.

543
00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:04.760
And he told me this like years ago, you know.

544
00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:09.140
And just, you know, when hairdressers just tell you their lore while they're doing your hair.

545
00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:11.900
And he's like, well, you know, I used to color Kathy Bates' hair.

546
00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:13.700
And oh, what a woman.

547
00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:16.140
And he just like so admired her and all this.

548
00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:19.680
He didn't gossip, but he just did name drop that he had colored her hair.

549
00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:27.940
So when I knew she was coming on the show, I had to resist that urge, you know.

550
00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:32.320
When like the second I saw her not to be like, we have the same hair coloriSt.

551
00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:34.220
Hi, I'm Jenna.

552
00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:35.540
We're our hair coloriSt.

553
00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:37.680
He colored your hair once.

554
00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:39.880
Welcome to the show.

555
00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:41.880
I'm so impressed that you suppressed that.

556
00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:44.440
I know that would come just tumbling out of my mouth.

557
00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:45.380
I held it.

558
00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:46.780
I can't remember for how long.

559
00:23:46.780 --> 00:23:49.340
I think I made it several days.

560
00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:56.100
And then I did finally say, you know, Robert Hickland, hair colorist?

561
00:23:56.500 --> 00:24:00.080
I think we, I think he, oh, yes, Bobby.

